artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $f:M\to M$ be a $C^2$ diffeomorphism of a compact Riemannian manifold $M$, and let $\Lambda\subset M$ be a partially hyperbolic attractor for $f$. Thus there is a continuous, $Df$-invariant splitting $T_\Lambda M = E^s\oplus E^c\oplus E^u$ such that $Df$ is uniformly contracting on $E^s$, uniformly expanding on $E^u$, and the rates on $E^c$ are dominated by those on $E^s$ and $E^u$; the strong unstable foliation $W^u$ tangent to $E^u$ is well defined.

An $f$-invariant Borel probability measure $\mu$ supported on $\Lambda$ is called a $u$-measure if its conditional measures on local strong unstable manifolds $W^u_{\mathrm{loc}}(x)$ are absolutely continuous with respect to the Riemannian volume induced on those manifolds. The central Lyapunov exponents of $\mu$ are the Lyapunov exponents of $Df$ restricted to $E^c$.

Assume:
(i) $\mu$ is a $u$-measure for $f$;
(ii) on a set of positive $\mu$-measure all central Lyapunov exponents are nonzero, and among them there exist both strictly positive and strictly negative central exponents;
(iii) for every $x\in\Lambda$ the global strong unstable manifold $W^u(x)$ is dense in $\Lambda$.

Under these hypotheses, determine whether:
(a) $\mu$ must be ergodic;
(b) $\mu$ must be the unique SRB measure for $f$;
(c) $f$ must be stably ergodic (i.e., every $C^2$ diffeomorphism sufficiently $C^1$-close to $f$ is ergodic with respect to its volume-class invariant measure on $\Lambda$).

